        "explanation": "UP means the interface is administratively enabled, while LOWER_UP means carrier is present on the layer below. UP without LOWER_UP and state DOWN is the enabled-but-no-carrier pattern, so the physical or virtual link is the suspect. The administratively disabled option is wrong because the UP flag is present. The DHCP failure option is wrong because it would produce a 169.254 address and does not explain a missing carrier. The MTU option is wrong because an MTU mismatch affects large packets on a working link and does not change the carrier state."
